note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note TWIN of unroll-sum.om with every unroll removed (contract section 4 line 91): OM-2
note unit, same expected stdout. Line numbers are those of unroll-sum.om plus one.
note Contract section 4 lines 87-92: for i T K unroll emits the body K times with i bound to 0..K-1,
note and removing unroll leaves behaviour unchanged (twin unroll-sum-rolled.om, same expectation).
note K = 1 (uint), 4 (uchar), 64 (ulong). Each loop folds i into an order-sensitive accumulator and
note the K = 64 loop also writes a[i] of a 65-element array, so K-1 or K+1 copies, a wrong binding of i
note or a reordering changes the printed lines (a K+1 copy writes a[64], read back below, never out of
note range). Expected stdout: oracle/s3s4/exp/unroll-sum.out (python3, oracle/s3s4/oracle.py).
om2
fn main to int
h = ulong 7
for i uint 1
h = add mul h 1000003 add ulong i 11
end
pu h
s = ulong 0
for i uchar 4
s = add mul s 131 add ulong i 3
end
pu s
a = new uchar 65 0
t = ulong 0
c = ulong 0
for i ulong 64
t = add mul t 6364136223846793005 add i 1442695040888963407
c = add c 1
put a i uchar and add mul i 37 5 255
end
pu t
pu c
q = ulong 0
for k ulong 65
q = add mul q 257 ulong get a k
end
pu q
ret 0
end
